\tag{fcap}
\tag{spin}
\tag{clifford}

\taxon{Definition}
\title{The Spin and Pin representations \citet{Section 3.2.1, pp. 55--56}{meinrenken2013clifford}}
\lean/tauceti{TauCeti.spinRep,TauCeti.pinRep}

\p{The groups #{\Spin(Q)} and #{\Pin(Q)} consist of units in the Clifford
algebra. Restricting the action #{\rho} of \ref{fcap-001K} along these two
inclusions gives representations on the same exterior carrier:

##{\operatorname{spinRep}:\Spin(Q)\longrightarrow\operatorname{Aut}_K(S),
\qquad
\operatorname{pinRep}:\Pin(Q)\longrightarrow\operatorname{Aut}_K(S).}

Meinrenken calls the restriction of a Clifford module to the Clifford group
the spin representation. The definitions here require only the commutative
ring, module, quadratic form, and polarization data already used for
#{\rho}; no nondegeneracy or finite-dimensionality is added.}
